@ben0112 thanks. Your C4A measurement is right and corrects our attribution. The 16×16 tiling belongs to the writers, not the model family: `indexer_k_quant_and_cache_triton` and the GLM-5.3 kpool writer tile when `block_size > 1`, while DeepSeek-V4's C4A compressor (`compress_norm_rope_store_triton`) writes token-major. Our "DeepSeek-V3.2/V4" wording above should have said `indexer_k_quant_and_cache_triton`.

We've sent the real-writer test as a regression test for your layout gate: https://github.com/ben0112/vllm/pull/1. It writes through the real writers (`indexer_k_quant_and_cache_triton` at block 1 and 64, and the C4A compressor), reads through the gated portable kernel and the torch fallback, and checks both the reader the gate picks per layout and the values against a writer-derived reference, including the tiled-cache negative case. On your branch as is, the test fails on tiled block-64 pages: the torch fallback the gate routes them to reads token-major (1.1 max rel, 0.031 top-32 overlap on gfx1030; we'd expect the same on gfx1151 without aiter). The PR's second commit fixes that, and you're welcome to drop it and fix it your own way.

The row-wise capture-safe verify variant will follow as its own PR, once it's rebuilt on main with tile-aware reads.

